{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For in six days YHWH made.</b> The intent of these [six days] is that man resemble his Creator as far as possible — through reflection, study, and chosen action, to find favor before Him." "<b>And He rested on the seventh day.</b> For on it was already completed all that is needed to bring the intended outcome to its end, and in perfection there is rest." "<b>Therefore YHWH blessed the Sabbath day.</b> With an added soul, which is an added capacity for the service of the blessed El." "<b>And He hallowed it.</b> That it be entirely for YHWH."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:30.192048007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}